WEBVTT

NOTE The narration of See the investment inside the house, generated by tools/captions.mjs from the voiceover's timing.

1
00:00:01.950 --> 00:00:04.400
You run a few houses by the room,

2
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.980
and you run them well.

3
00:00:05.980 --> 00:00:07.950
Now you've found the next one,

4
00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.830
a six-bedroom house near the greenway.

5
00:00:11.530 --> 00:00:15.020
So you work it out the way everyone does: rooms,

6
00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:18.380
times weekly rent, times occupancy.

7
00:00:18.380 --> 00:00:20.430
That's the right formula.

8
00:00:20.430 --> 00:00:22.430
But you picked the rent yourself,

9
00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:24.930
and the ninety percent is a guess.

10
00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.060
And nobody has counted the other

11
00:00:27.060 --> 00:00:29.980
houses renting rooms nearby.

12
00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.890
You make the offer on those numbers,

13
00:00:32.890 --> 00:00:35.010
and the house is yours.

14
00:00:35.110 --> 00:00:37.320
Then the rooms go up for rent,

15
00:00:37.320 --> 00:00:40.110
and two of them sit empty for weeks.

16
00:00:40.510 --> 00:00:42.960
Seventeen other houses within three

17
00:00:42.960 --> 00:00:46.070
miles were renting rooms all along.

18
00:00:47.070 --> 00:00:50.080
If your rooms fill seventy-five percent

19
00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:53.200
of the time instead of ninety percent,

20
00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:53.520
that's seven hundred eighty-three

21
00:00:53.520 --> 00:00:57.430
dollars a month off your plan.

22
00:00:57.530 --> 00:01:00.380
The formula was fine all along.

23
00:01:00.380 --> 00:01:04.180
The numbers inside it just had nothing behind them.

24
00:01:05.180 --> 00:01:09.630
RoomIQ puts evidence behind each of those numbers,

25
00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:11.450
before you make the offer.

26
00:01:11.650 --> 00:01:13.380
Type in the address,

27
00:01:13.380 --> 00:01:15.700
and it counts and maps the co-living

28
00:01:15.700 --> 00:01:18.250
houses within about three miles.

29
00:01:18.250 --> 00:01:20.780
Add each room and its bath,

30
00:01:20.780 --> 00:01:22.940
and the rent and occupancy come

31
00:01:22.940 --> 00:01:25.370
from comparable rooms nearby.

32
00:01:25.370 --> 00:01:28.380
Then it prints the estimate with its formula,

33
00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:32.330
its comps, and a label for how sure it is.

34
00:01:32.930 --> 00:01:36.900
So you're back at the same table with the same formula,

35
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.220
and every number has its evidence beside it.

36
00:01:40.220 --> 00:01:42.590
You read the label before the number,

37
00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:45.630
and you test the deal with your own costs.

38
00:01:45.630 --> 00:01:47.280
Then you make the offer,

39
00:01:47.280 --> 00:01:49.750
knowing what each number rests on.

40
00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:54.800
RoomIQ. See the investment inside the house.
